Significance: minor
Type: added

A new Email page in the Events menu lets an administrator message users without going through an event: all users, users with chosen roles, or, while RSVPs are turned on, users who RSVP'd to any event in the past 1, 3, 6 or 12 months. Users who turned event updates off in their profile are skipped, delivery runs on cron in batches so the page returns right away and a large user base is not sent in a single request, and the audience, batch size, and subject line are filterable through `gatherpress_site_message_recipients`, `gatherpress_site_message_batch_size`, and `gatherpress_site_message_subject`.

A shared `Mailer` class now owns how every GatherPress email is sent and queued, through `send()` for one recipient and `bulk_send()` for a list. `gatherpress_mail_recipient_consent` lets a site decide per recipient, per mail path, whether a message goes out. It defaults to the event updates opt-in, except for emails about a user's own RSVP (the `rsvp` path), which go out unless the filter says otherwise. `gatherpress_mail_pre_enqueue_job` lets a companion plugin take over job scheduling.

The profile opt-in now names the post type users actually hear about (the one that takes RSVPs) instead of always saying "events", so a site can change the wording through the post type's own labels.
